---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const SEO_TITLE = "About Us — PdfAndImg";
---

<style>
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .about-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr !important;
    }
  }
</style>

<Layout title={SEO_TITLE}>
  <section class="relative z-20 pt-20 container-stripe">
    
    <!-- Hero Header centered -->
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <div
        style="
          display: inline-flex;
          align-items: center;
          gap: 8px;
          background: rgba(200,241,53,0.08);
          border: 1px solid rgba(200,241,53,0.2);
          border-radius: 100px;
          padding: 5px 14px;
          margin-bottom: 24px;
        "
      >
        <span
          style="
            font-family: var(--font-mono);
            font-size: 0.6875rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.1em;
            color: var(--color-lime);
          "
        >About Us</span>
      </div>

      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 4.5rem); line-height: 1.05; margin: 0 0 24px; letter-spacing: -0.04em;">
        About <br/>
        <span style="color: var(--color-lime);">PdfAndImg.</span>
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--color-ink-2); line-height: 1.6; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto;">
        PdfAndImg is a comprehensive suite of <strong>44 precision micro-tools</strong>. What started as an advanced binary-search image compressor has evolved into a complete, zero-server framework for PDF manipulation, HEIC conversion, and pixel-perfect cropping.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Tech Grid centered -->
    <div
      style="
        max-width: 960px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
        gap: 1px;
        background: var(--color-border);
        border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
        border-radius: 20px;
        overflow: hidden;
      "
      class="about-grid"
    >
      
      <div style="background: var(--color-surface-1); padding: 48px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px;">
        <div style="width: 48px; height: 48px; background: var(--color-surface-3); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-hi); border-radius: 12px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-lime)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 16V12"/><path d="M12 8h.01"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700;">The Problem</h3>
        <p style="color: var(--color-ink-2); font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7;">
          Most image compressors use generic "Quality" sliders. For users filling out forms with strict KB limits, this is inefficient. You don't care about a "70%" setting; you care about staying under a 20KB or 100KB limit.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="background: var(--color-surface-1); padding: 48px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px;">
        <div style="width: 48px; height: 48px; background: var(--color-surface-3); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-hi); border-radius: 12px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-lime)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2v20M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700;">Binary Search Solution</h3>
        <p style="color: var(--color-ink-2); font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7;">
          We developed a unique Smart Image Compressor algorithm. It automatically tests dozens of quality variations in local memory to find the mathematically highest fidelity that fits exactly inside your target file size.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="background: var(--color-surface-1); padding: 48px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px;">
        <div style="width: 48px; height: 48px; background: var(--color-surface-3); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-hi); border-radius: 12px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-lime)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 16V8a2 2 0 0 0-2-2H5a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h14a2 2 0 0 0 2-2z"/><path d="M7 10l2 2 2-2"/><path d="M13 14l2-2 2 2"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700;">Dual-Mode Engine</h3>
        <p style="color: var(--color-ink-2); font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7;">
          Not just for shrinking — our engine can also enhance small images to meet minimum size requirements. By combining high-fidelity upscaling with metadata padding, we ensure your files meet strict portal minimums without quality degradation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="background: var(--color-surface-1); padding: 48px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px;">
        <div style="width: 48px; height: 48px; background: var(--color-surface-3); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-hi); border-radius: 12px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-lime)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"/><line x1="9" y1="3" x2="9" y2="21"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700;">Instant Bulk Processing</h3>
        <p style="color: var(--color-ink-2); font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7;">
          Save time by uploading multiple images at once. Our engine processes them in batches locally on your device and outputs a convenient ZIP file containing all your perfectly sized images.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="background: var(--color-surface-1); padding: 48px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px;">
        <div style="width: 48px; height: 48px; background: var(--color-surface-3); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-hi); border-radius: 12px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-lime)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h14"/><path d="M18 22V8a2 2 0 0 0-2-2H2"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700;">Crop Image Onlineping</h3>
        <p style="color: var(--color-ink-2); font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7;">
          Signature and passport photo requirements often demand specific aspect ratios. Our integrated cropping tool provides presets for Square, Portrait, and Wide-Signature formats to ensure you meet dimensional specs before you compress.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="background: var(--color-surface-1); padding: 48px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px;">
        <div style="width: 48px; height: 48px; background: var(--color-surface-3); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-hi); border-radius: 12px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-lime)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M22 19a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5l2 3h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700;">Optimized for Portals</h3>
        <p style="color: var(--color-ink-2); font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7;">
          Whether it's SSC, UPSC, or a Bank IBPS portal, our tool is tuned for the exact quirks of government upload systems. We handle the metadata and file headers to guarantee 100% acceptance rates.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="background: var(--color-surface-1); padding: 48px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; align-items: center; text-align: center;">
        <div style="width: 48px; height: 48px; background: var(--color-surface-3); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-hi); border-radius: 12px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-lime)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700;">100% Privacy</h3>
        <p style="color: var(--color-ink-2); font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7;">
          By leveraging the modern Browser Canvas API, all processing happens locally on your hardware. Your photos never leave your device, making PdfAndImg the safest choice for ID documents.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="background: var(--color-surface-1); padding: 48px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; align-items: center; text-align: center;">
        <div style="width: 48px; height: 48px; background: var(--color-surface-3); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-hi); border-radius: 12px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-lime)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"></path><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"></polyline><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"></line><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"></line><polyline points="10 9 9 9 8 9"></polyline></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700;">PDF Packaging</h3>
        <p style="color: var(--color-ink-2); font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7;">
          Need to submit a photo as a document? Our suite seamlessly converts any JPG, PNG, or WEBP directly into perfectly formatted PDF documents right in your browser, maintaining zero-server confidentiality.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="background: var(--color-surface-1); padding: 48px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; align-items: center; text-align: center; grid-column: 1 / -1;">
        <div style="width: 48px; height: 48px; background: var(--color-surface-3); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-hi); border-radius: 12px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-lime)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"></path><polyline points="17 8 12 3 7 8"></polyline><line x1="12" y1="3" x2="12" y2="15"></line></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700;">PDF Page Remover</h3>
        <p style="color: var(--color-ink-2); font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto;">
          Our highly-requested PDF Page Remover tool allows you to securely delete unwanted or confidential pages from any document instantly. Built with Bank-Grade Security to ensure complete privacy.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- Footer Note centered -->
    <div style="max-width: 960px; margin: 80px auto 0; padding-top: 40px; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
      <p style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--color-ink-3);">© 2026 PdfAndImg</p>
      <a href="/" class="nav-link">← Return to Interface</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
